. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         /*
>         The item plh0004, “Political attitude: In politics, people often talk
>  about ‘left’ and ‘right’ when it comes to characterizing different political
>  attitudes. 
>         Thinking about your own political views, where would you place yourse
> lf?”, serves as an appropriate measure of left-leaning political preferences.
>  It is 
>         measured on a scale from 0 to 10, where 0 indicates a far-left positi
> on and 10 a far-right position. To facilitate interpretation, the variable ha
> s been 
>         reverse-coded such that higher values reflect more left-leaning polit
> ical preferences. Specifically, the transformed variable plh0004_R is defined
>  as 
>         plh0004_R = 10 – plh0004. 
> 
>         This item is available in the 2005, 2009, 2014, and 2019 waves of the
>  survey, enabling the use of panel data methods. Accordingly, the estimation 
> relies on a 
>         fixed-effects specification with standard errors clustered at the res
> pondent level to account for within-individual correlation across waves
>         */
. 
.         xtset pid syear

Panel variable: pid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2005 to 2019, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

.         xtreg plh0004_R has_daughters has_kids age i.pgisced11 i.pgfamstd i.s
> year, fe cluster(pid)
note: 1.pgisced11 omitted because of collinearity.
note: 5.pgisced11 omitted because of collinearity.
note: 7.pgfamstd omitted because of collinearity.
note: 2019.syear omitted because of collinearity.

